<div class="panel updates">
  <h1 class="article__title listing__title">Updates</h1>
  <p class="updates__lede">The articles are the old site's and do not change. What the
    archive can still serve of what they point at does.</p>

  <h2 class="stock__title">Dead links left</h2>
  <ul class="stock">
    <% Ofpr::DeadLinks::KINDS.each do |kind, label| %><li>
      <p class="stock__count"><%= number(Ofpr::DeadLinks.count(kind)) %></p>
      <p class="stock__label"><%= label %></p>
      <p class="stock__note">of <%= number(Ofpr::DeadLinks.linked(kind)) %> linked</p>
    </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
  <p class="stock__get"><a href="/dead-links.tsv" download>Download the list</a>, every
    one of them with an article that asks for it. If you have a file on an old drive,
    the report link below is the way in.</p>

  <section class="update">
    <p class="update__date"><time datetime="2026-11-09">9 November 2026</time></p>
    <h2 class="update__title">238 files back out of the archives</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>100 downloads, 68 pictures and 70 files and pages from the hosted
        sites</strong> restored, 2.9 GB of them, out of the Wayback Machine, GameFront's
        mirror and a private archive of the old file sites.</li>
      <li>15 are the nearest surviving copy rather than the release named, and 2 are
        damaged, kept the way the only source left serves them.</li>
      <li>A download that needs other addons now lists them, each one linked.</li>
      <li>What is left was nearly all on <code>ofp.gamepark.cz</code>, which no web
        archive ever crawled.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="update">
    <p class="update__date"><time datetime="2026-11-08">8 November 2026</time></p>
    <h2 class="update__title">The archive is back</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>10,245 articles</strong> at the addresses they were published at:
        news from 2001 to 2019, addons, missions, MODS, patches and utilities.</li>
      <li>Old <code>index.php?showthis=</code> links still land on the right article,
        and <a href="<%= page_url('/convert') %>">Convert</a> looks one up.</li>
      <li>Rebuilt pages: readable on a phone, a dark theme that follows the system,
        pictures that open where they are, linked videos playing in place.</li>
      <li>Search across every title, body and author, and the files served from
        <a href="https://ofpisnotdead.com/">ofpisnotdead.com</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>
